From b4869d56a407151d6ca0b2ca45178423fc262d0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:06:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ci: publish the debug-assertions corpus gate's artifacts,
 and document why both assertions-ON runs exist

The 'Regression corpus (debug-assertions compiler)' step writes
regression-dbgassert-results.{json,log}, but 'Upload regression results'
ran BEFORE the corpus step and did not list the two files - a failing
closing gate produced no downloadable evidence. Move the upload step to
the very end of the job (after the corpus flip, which is the last step
that uses the compiler binary) and add both files to its path list; with
if: always() the gate's JSON/log now publish even when the gate itself
fails.

Document, in the corpus step's comment, why the second assertions-ON run
is not a duplicate of 'Run tests (debug-assertions on)': the unit step
exercises every pass's in-process debug-only invariant, the corpus step
exercises the validator end-to-end over real codegen dataflow through the
compiler binary. Dropping either silently unobserves that layer's
contract; the build cost is shared (same profile override, cache hit),
and the marginal cost of keeping both is the corpus runtime itself.

1 file, +34/-16.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index f807ce94..eb7ba14d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -657,18 +657,6 @@ jobs:
       - name: Verify kernel tool-identity invalidation
         run: bash tests/regression/check_kernel_tool_identity.sh
 
-      - name: Upload regression results
-        if: always()
-        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7
-        with:
-          name: regression-results
-          path: |
-            regression-results.json
-            regression-results.log
-            ci-regression-environment.txt
-            inline-asm-utf8.json
-          if-no-files-found: warn
-
       # Deterministic bounded fuzzing catches parser/linker panics without
       # making ordinary PRs depend on an unbounded corpus or external fuzzer.
       - name: Run linker fuzz smoke
@@ -691,10 +679,21 @@ jobs:
       # fingerprints, so the earlier gates' artifacts stay cached) and
       # re-runs the SSA-validated regression corpus against real codegen.
       # It runs LAST deliberately: the assertions-ON binary overwrites the
-      # target/fastbuild/lccc path, and no later step in this job uses it.
-      # A missed invalidate_acc() on any corpus-covered dataflow now fails
-      # CI here - loudly, naming the value, both epochs, and the last
-      # unclassified emitted line.
+      # target/fastbuild/lccc path, and no later step in this job USES it -
+      # only the artifact upload follows, and `if: always()` publishes this
+      # step's JSON/log even when it fails (a gate that fails without its
+      # artifacts is a report without evidence). A missed invalidate_acc()
+      # on any corpus-covered dataflow now fails CI here - loudly, naming
+      # the value, both epochs, and the last unclassified emitted line.
+      #
+      # NOT a duplicate of "Run tests (debug-assertions on)": that step
+      # exercises the in-process unit suite (every pass's debug-only
+      # invariant); this one exercises the validator end-to-end over real
